# 必考词 Unit27
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit27核心词汇

{{maximize}}{{/ˈmæksɪmaɪz}}{{v. 使最大化； maximize；充分利用}}{{The company aims to maximize profits.}}
{{mechanism}}{{/ˈmekənɪzəm}}{{n. 机制； mechanism；机械装置}}{{The clock has a complex mechanism.}}
{{media}}{{/ˈmiːdiə}}{{n. 媒体； media；媒介}}{{Social media has changed the way we communicate.}}
{{mediate}}{{/ˈmiːdieɪt}}{{v. 调解； mediate；居中促成}}{{The UN mediated between the two countries.}}
{{medieval}}{{/ˌmediˈiːvl}}{{adj. 中世纪的； medieval；古老的}}{{The town has a well-preserved medieval castle.}}
{{memo}}{{/ˈmeməʊ}}{{n. 备忘录； memo}}{{The manager sent a memo to all employees.}}
{{mental}}{{/ˈmentl}}{{adj. 精神的； mental；心理的}}{{Mental health is as important as physical health.}}
{{mentor}}{{/ˈmentɔːr}}{{n./v. 导师； mentor；指导}}{{She has been a mentor to many young scientists.}}
{{merchant}}{{/ˈmɜːtʃənt}}{{n. 商人； merchant；零售商}}{{The merchant sold goods from all over the world.}}
{{mercy}}{{/ˈmɜːsi}}{{n. 仁慈； mercy；幸运}}{{The judge showed mercy to the first-time offender.}}
{{merge}}{{/mɜːdʒ}}{{v. 合并； merge；融合}}{{The two companies merged to form a larger corporation.}}
{{merit}}{{/ˈmerɪt}}{{n./v. 优点； merit；值得}}{{The plan has considerable merit.}}
{{method}}{{/ˈmeθəd}}{{n. 方法； method；办法}}{{We need to find a more efficient method.}}
{{migrate}}{{/maɪˈɡreɪt}}{{v. 迁移； migrate；迁徙}}{{Many birds migrate south in winter.}}
{{military}}{{/ˈmɪlɪtəri}}{{adj./n. 军事的； military；军队}}{{The country increased its military spending.}}
{{minister}}{{/ˈmɪnɪstər}}{{n. 部长； minister；牧师}}{{The prime minister addressed the nation.}}
{{minor}}{{/ˈmaɪnər}}{{adj./n. 次要的； minor；未成年人}}{{The problem is minor and can be easily fixed.}}
{{minority}}{{/maɪˈnɒrəti}}{{n. 少数； minority；少数民族}}{{The rights of minorities should be protected.}}
{{miracle}}{{/ˈmɪrəkl}}{{n. 奇迹； miracle}}{{It was a miracle that no one was hurt.}}
{{mislead}}{{/ˌmɪsˈliːd}}{{v. 误导； mislead；欺骗}}{{The advertisement was designed to mislead consumers.}}
{{mission}}{{/ˈmɪʃn}}{{n. 使命； mission；代表团}}{{The mission to Mars was a great success.}}
{{mobile}}{{/ˈməʊbaɪl}}{{adj./n. 移动的； mobile；手机}}{{Mobile phones have become essential in daily life.}}
{{moderate}}{{/ˈmɒdərət}}{{adj./v. 适度的； moderate；缓和}}{{Moderate exercise is beneficial to health.}}
{{modify}}{{/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ}}{{v. 修改； modify；改变}}{{We need to modify the plan.}}
{{momentum}}{{/məˈmentəm}}{{n. 动力； momentum；势头}}{{The reform movement gained momentum.}}
{{monitor}}{{/ˈmɒnɪtər}}{{n./v. 监视器； monitor；监控}}{{Doctors monitor the patient's condition closely.}}
{{monopoly}}{{/məˈnɒpəli}}{{n. 垄断； monopoly；独占}}{{The company has a monopoly on the market.}}
{{moral}}{{/ˈmɒrəl}}{{adj./n. 道德的； moral；寓意}}{{The story has a strong moral lesson.}}
{{moreover}}{{/mɔːrˈəʊvər}}{{adv. 此外； moreover；而且}}{{The plan is feasible; moreover, it is cost-effective.}}
{{mortgage}}{{/ˈmɔːɡɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 抵押； mortgage；按揭}}{{They took out a mortgage to buy their first home.}}
{{motivate}}{{/ˈməʊtɪveɪt}}{{v. 激励； motivate；促动}}{{Good teachers motivate students to learn.}}
{{motive}}{{/ˈməʊtɪv}}{{n. 动机； motive；目的}}{{The police are investigating the motive for the crime.}}
{{multiple}}{{/ˈmʌltɪpl}}{{adj. 多重的； multiple；多个的}}{{The test has multiple-choice questions.}}
{{multitude}}{{/ˈmʌltɪtjuːd}}{{n. 大量； multitude；众多}}{{A multitude of problems arose during the project.}}
{{mutual}}{{/ˈmjuːtʃuəl}}{{adj. 相互的； mutual；共同的}}{{They have a mutual respect for each other.}}
{{narrate}}{{/ˈnæreɪt}}{{v. 叙述； narrate；讲述}}{{She narrated the story of her childhood.}}
{{navigate}}{{/ˈnævɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 导航； navigate；航行}}{{It is difficult to navigate through the fog.}}
{{negotiate}}{{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt}}{{v. 谈判； negotiate；协商}}{{The unions negotiated a pay rise for workers.}}
{{neutral}}{{/ˈnjuːtrəl}}{{adj. 中立的； neutral；中性的}}{{Switzerland remained neutral during the war.}}
{{nevertheless}}{{/ˌnevəðəˈles}}{{adv. 然而； nevertheless；不过}}{{The task was difficult; nevertheless, he completed it.}}
{{nominal}}{{/ˈnɒmɪnl}}{{adj. 名义上的； nominal；微不足道的}}{{He holds a nominal position in the company.}}
{{nominate}}{{/ˈnɒmɪneɪt}}{{v. 提名； nominate；任命}}{{She was nominated for the best actress award.}}
{{norm}}{{/nɔːm}}{{n. 标准； norm；规范}}{{Working from home has become the norm.}}
{{notable}}{{/ˈnəʊtəbl}}{{adj. 值得注意的； notable；显著的}}{{The town is notable for its architecture.}}
{{notion}}{{/ˈnəʊʃn}}{{n. 概念； notion；想法}}{{The notion that the earth is flat has been disproven.}}
{{nourish}}{{/ˈnʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 养育； nourish；滋养}}{{Good food nourishes the body and mind.}}
{{novel}}{{/ˈnɒvl}}{{adj./n. 新奇的； novel；小说}}{{She came up with a novel approach.}}
{{nuclear}}{{/ˈnjuːkliər}}{{adj. 核的； nuclear；原子能的}}{{Nuclear energy is a controversial topic.}}
{{numerous}}{{/ˈnjuːmərəs}}{{adj. 众多的； numerous}}{{Numerous studies confirm the finding.}}
{{nurture}}{{/ˈnɜːtʃər}}{{v./n. 养育； nurture；培养}}{{Parents should nurture their children's talents.}}
{{nutrition}}{{/njuˈtrɪʃn}}{{n. 营养； nutrition；营养学}}{{Proper nutrition is essential for growth.}}
{{obey}}{{/əˈbeɪ}}{{v. 服从； obey；遵守}}{{Citizens should obey the law.}}
{{objective}}{{/əbˈdʒektɪv}}{{n./adj. 目标； objective；客观的}}{{The main objective is to reduce costs.}}
{{obligation}}{{/ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn}}{{n. 义务； obligation；责任}}{{You are under no obligation to accept.}}
{{obscure}}{{/əbˈskjʊər}}{{adj./v. 模糊的； obscure；使模糊}}{{The meaning of the text is obscure.}}
{{observe}}{{/əbˈzɜːv}}{{v. 观察； observe；遵守}}{{Scientists observe the behavior of animals.}}
{{obsolete}}{{/ˈɒbsəliːt}}{{adj. 过时的； obsolete}}{{The old technology has become obsolete.}}
{{obstacle}}{{/ˈɒbstəkl}}{{n. 障碍； obstacle；阻碍}}{{Lack of funding is a major obstacle.}}
{{obtain}}{{/əbˈteɪn}}{{v. 获得； obtain；得到}}{{She obtained a degree in engineering.}}
{{obvious}}{{/ˈɒbviəs}}{{adj. 明显的； obvious}}{{The answer was obvious to everyone.}}
{{occupy}}{{/ˈɒkjupaɪ}}{{v. 占据； occupy；使忙碌}}{{The meeting occupied the entire morning.}}
{{occur}}{{/əˈkɜːr}}{{v. 发生； occur；出现}}{{The accident occurred at the intersection.}}
{{offend}}{{/əˈfend}}{{v. 冒犯； offend；违反}}{{I'm sorry if I offended you.}}
{{offset}}{{/ˈɒfset}}{{v./n. 抵消； offset；补偿}}{{The gains offset the losses.}}
{{ongoing}}{{/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ}}{{adj. 进行中的； ongoing}}{{The investigation is still ongoing.}}
{{operate}}{{/ˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 操作； operate；运转}}{{The machine is easy to operate.}}
{{opponent}}{{/əˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 对手； opponent；反对者}}{{She defeated her opponent in the election.}}
{{opportunity}}{{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti}}{{n. 机会； opportunity}}{{This is a great opportunity for growth.}}
{{oppose}}{{/əˈpəʊz}}{{v. 反对； oppose；对抗}}{{Many citizens opposed the new policy.}}
{{optimistic}}{{/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk}}{{adj. 乐观的； optimistic}}{{He is optimistic about the future.}}
{{orient}}{{/ˈɔːrient}}{{v. 使适应； orient；朝向}}{{The program helps students orient themselves.}}
{{origin}}{{/ˈɒrɪdʒɪn}}{{n. 起源； origin；出身}}{{The origin of the custom dates back centuries.}}
{{original}}{{/əˈrɪdʒənl}}{{adj./n. 原始的； original；原件}}{{The original painting is in the museum.}}
{{outcome}}{{/ˈaʊtkʌm}}{{n. 结果； outcome；成果}}{{The outcome of the election was unexpected.}}
{{outlook}}{{/ˈaʊtlʊk}}{{n. 展望； outlook；观点}}{{The economic outlook is positive.}}
{{output}}{{/ˈaʊtpʊt}}{{n. 产量； output；输出}}{{The factory's output has doubled.}}
{{outrage}}{{/ˈaʊtreɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 愤怒； outrage；暴行}}{{The decision sparked public outrage.}}
{{overall}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈɔːl}}{{adj./adv. 总体的； overall；总的来说}}{{The overall quality is excellent.}}
{{overcome}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈkʌm}}{{v. 克服； overcome；战胜}}{{She overcame many challenges.}}
{{overlook}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈlʊk}}{{v. 忽视； overlook；俯瞰}}{{Don't overlook the small details.}}
{{overseas}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈsiːz}}{{adj./adv. 海外的； overseas}}{{Many students study overseas.}}
{{overt}}{{/əʊˈvɜːt}}{{adj. 公开的； overt；明显的}}{{There was no overt sign of hostility.}}
{{overwhelm}}{{/ˌəʊvərˈwelm}}{{v. 压倒； overwhelm；使不知所措}}{{She was overwhelmed by the response.}}
{{pace}}{{/peɪs}}{{n. 步伐； pace；速度}}{{The pace of change is accelerating.}}
{{panel}}{{/ˈpænl}}{{n. 面板； panel；专家组}}{{A panel of experts reviewed the proposal.}}
{{paradox}}{{/ˈpærədɒks}}{{n. 矛盾； paradox；悖论}}{{It is a paradox that wealth can cause unhappiness.}}
{{parallel}}{{/ˈpærəlel}}{{adj./n. 平行的； parallel；类似}}{{The two roads run parallel to each other.}}
{{participate}}{{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 参与； participate}}{{All students are encouraged to participate.}}
{{particular}}{{/pəˈtɪkjələr}}{{adj. 特定的； particular；挑剔的}}{{Is there a particular reason you're asking?}}
{{patent}}{{/ˈpætnt}}{{n./adj. 专利； patent；明显的}}{{The company holds several patents.}}
{{pattern}}{{/ˈpætn}}{{n. 模式； pattern；图案}}{{Scientists have identified a pattern.}}
{{peculiar}}{{/pɪˈkjuːliər}}{{adj. 独特的； peculiar；奇怪的}}{{There was something peculiar about his behavior.}}
{{perceive}}{{/pəˈsiːv}}{{v. 感知； perceive；认为}}{{The problem is perceived as serious.}}
{{permanent}}{{/ˈpɜːmənənt}}{{adj. 永久的； permanent}}{{She found a permanent job.}}
{{permit}}{{/pəˈmɪt}}{{v./n. 允许； permit；许可证}}{{Smoking is not permitted here.}}
{{persist}}{{/pəˈsɪst}}{{v. 坚持； persist；持续}}{{He persisted despite the difficulties.}}
{{perspective}}{{/pəˈspektɪv}}{{n. 观点； perspective；视角}}{{Try to see it from a different perspective.}}
{{pervasive}}{{/pəˈveɪsɪv}}{{adj. 普遍的； pervasive；弥漫的}}{{Social media is pervasive in modern life.}}
{{petition}}{{/pəˈtɪʃn}}{{n./v. 请愿； petition；申请}}{{They signed a petition to save the park.}}
{{phenomenon}}{{/fəˈnɒmɪnən}}{{n. 现象； phenomenon}}{{Climate change is a global phenomenon.}}
{{pioneer}}{{/ˌpaɪəˈnɪər}}{{n./v. 先驱； pioneer；开拓}}{{She was a pioneer in computer science.}}
